{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"smith","type":"text","text":"# Mark S. Smith\nb. 1956 · Princeton Seminary\n\n**The consensus leader**\nIsraelite religion = subset of Canaanite\n\n*The Early History of God* (1990)\n*The Origins of Biblical Monotheism* (2001)\n\nPhD: Yale (Pope), studied under Cross at HDS\nRoman Catholic — argues against his tradition\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]\n[[notes/theology/meta-analysis-scholars]]","x":350,"y":-2880,"width":300,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"lewis","type":"text","text":"# Theodore J. Lewis\nJohns Hopkins Univ.\n\n**Monumental reference**\n\n*The Origin and Character of God*\n(2020, Oxford UP) — 1,000+ pages\n\nDefinitive reference work;\ncomprehensive synthesis\nof text, archaeology, iconography\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":-190,"y":-4155,"width":300,"height":240,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"levenson","type":"text","text":"# Jon D. Levenson\nHarvard Divinity School\n\n**Critique of criticism**\n\n\"Unexamined Commitments of\nCriticism\" (1993, First Things):\n\nHistorical criticism has its own\nunexamined faith commitments\n\nJewish and Catholic interpretive\ntraditions erased by methods\nrooted in Protestant *sola scriptura*\n\n*Sinai and Zion* (1985)\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":2990,"y":-3280,"width":300,"height":290,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"fleming","type":"text","text":"# Daniel E. Fleming\nNew York University\n\n**Complicates Kenite hypothesis**\n\n*Yahweh Before Israel* (2021, Cambridge UP)\n\nYahweh was NOT imported\nfrom outsiders — the divine name\nreflects Israel's own diverse origins\n\nAmong most recent major treatments\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":2795,"y":-2160,"width":300,"height":260,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"ecosystem-critical","type":"text","text":"## Critical / Mainline Ecosystem\n\n**Primary Organization:**\nSBL (Society of Biblical Literature)\n\n**Key Journals:**\nJBL · VT · JSOT · CBQ · ZAW\n\n**Key Institutions:**\nHarvard · Yale · Chicago · Johns Hopkins\nNYU · Princeton · UPenn · Columbia\nBerkeley · Brown\n\n**De facto requirement:**\nMethodological naturalism\n\n**Publishers:**\nOxford · Cambridge · Brill\nEerdmans (bridge)\n\n[[notes/theology/meta-analysis-scholars]]","x":800,"y":-610,"width":310,"height":320,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"stavrakopoulou","type":"text","text":"# Francesca Stavrakopoulou\nb. 1975 · Univ. of Exeter\n\n**Atheist · Humanists UK patron**\n\n*God: An Anatomy* (2021)\n\nYahweh had a human-shaped body —\nwalks, talks, weeps, laughs, eats,\nsleeps, undeniably male\n\nPantheon reduction, not revelation\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":2340,"y":-2570,"width":300,"height":250,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"ecosystem-bridge","type":"text","text":"## Bridge Ecosystem\n\n**Organization:**\nIBR (Institute for Biblical Research)\n\n**Journal:**\nBBR (Bulletin for Biblical Research)\n\n**Publisher:**\nEerdmans — publishes BOTH\ncritical (Smith, Dever)\nAND evangelical (Block, Walton)\n\n**ETS/SBL Co-location (since 2008):**\nSame city, same week\nEvangelicals attend both\nDeliberate strategy to prevent isolation\n\n\"Threshold figures\":\nBauckham · N.T. Wright · Wenham\nLongman · Block\n\n[[notes/theology/meta-analysis-scholars]]","x":40,"y":635,"width":310,"height":340,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"schmid","type":"text","text":"# Konrad Schmid\nUniv. of Zurich\n\n**Late-dating challenge**\nPentateuch shaped in Persian period\n(5th–4th c. BCE), not pre-exilic\n\nJ source = exilic/post-exilic\n\nIf correct: biblical texts can't be\nused as windows into pre-exilic polytheism\n\n*The Old Testament: A Literary History* (2012)\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":-1410,"y":-3620,"width":300,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"albright","type":"text","text":"# William F. Albright\n1891–1971 · Johns Hopkins\n\n**Early Mosaic monotheism**\nIsrael distinctive from the beginning\n\n12 confirmed doctoral students:\nBright, Freedman, Cross, Wright...\n\nRoots in German philology\n(Delitzsch via Paul Haupt)\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":-2820,"y":-2990,"width":300,"height":260,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"kratz","type":"text","text":"# Reinhard Kratz\nUniv. of Göttingen\n\n**German historical-critical school**\n\nHistorical vs. biblical Israel\nCompositional history\n\nEuropean rigorous criticism;\nlate dating of sources\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":-960,"y":-2770,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"romer","type":"text","text":"# Thomas Römer\nCollège de France / Lausanne\n\n**Europe's leading voice**\n\n*The Invention of God* (2015, Harvard UP)\n\nYahweh emerged in Edom/Arabia\nas wilderness/storm/war god\n\nMonotheism \"in fits and starts\"\n— not complete until after exile\n\nOne of the most prestigious\nacademic chairs in the world\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":1630,"y":-1290,"width":300,"height":290,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"wright","type":"text","text":"# G. Ernest Wright\n1909–1974 · Harvard\n\n**Albright's student**\nBiblical archaeology pioneer\n\nAdvisor to William Dever\nBrought ANE archaeology\ninto biblical studies\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":-2820,"y":-1290,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"finkelstein","type":"text","text":"# Israel Finkelstein\nb. 1949 · Tel Aviv Univ.\n\n**Low Chronology**\nUnited Monarchy far smaller\nthan Bible describes\n\nYahwism developed in two\nseparate kingdoms with\ndifferent religious trajectories\n\n*The Bible Unearthed* (2001)\nDan David Prize (2005)\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":-2970,"y":185,"width":300,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"cross","type":"text","text":"# Frank Moore Cross\n1921–2012 · Harvard\nHancock Prof. of Hebrew (1958–1992)\n\n**Yahweh emerged within El tradition**\nEvolutionary model; early distinctiveness\n\n*Canaanite Myth and Hebrew Epic* (1973)\n\n6 doctoral students:\nFriedman, Stager, Davila, Seow...\n\nIntellectual heir to Albright\nPresbyterian background\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":-1260,"y":-430,"width":300,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"friedman","type":"text","text":"# Richard Elliott Friedman\nb. ? · Univ. of Georgia\n\n**Cross's student (ThD Harvard)**\n\n*Who Wrote the Bible?* (1987)\n*The Exodus* (2017)\n\nLevite Exodus Hypothesis:\nOnly Levites escaped Egypt;\nmonotheism via this specific group\n\nMiddle position between\nKaufmann and Smith\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":-1410,"y":1150,"width":300,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"dever","type":"text","text":"# William G. Dever\nb. 1933 · Arizona (Emeritus)\n\n**\"Not even a theist\"**\n\nArchaeology-first\nThousands of JPFs, multiple shrines\n\nFolk religion was thoroughly\npolytheistic well into monarchy\n\n*Did God Have a Wife?* (2005)\n*Has Archaeology Buried the Bible?* (2020)\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":-2160,"y":-900,"width":300,"height":290,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"thompson","type":"text","text":"# Thomas L. Thompson\nCopenhagen (Emeritus)\n\n**Minimalist**\n\nBiblical Israel is fiction\nHebrew Bible = Persian/\nHellenistic literary creation\n\n*The Mythic Past* (1999)\n\nUndermines BOTH evolution\nAND early monotheism\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":2340,"y":-150,"width":300,"height":240,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"heiser-isolation","type":"text","text":"## Heiser Isolation\n\n**The puzzle:**\n\nPhD from UW-Madison (legit secular)\n\nTextual arguments on Deut 32:8-9\n**identical** to critical consensus\n\nYet almost entirely **ignored**\nin critical scholarship\n\n**Why?**\n- Works for Faithlife, not a university\n- Publishes with Lexham, not Oxford\n- Confessional: evangelical inerrantist\n- Popular audience (*The Unseen Realm*)\n- Conclusions align with his faith\n  community's preferences\n\n**Counter:** If his textual arguments\nare sound, dismissal looks like\ninstitutional gatekeeping, not\nscholarly evaluation\n\n[[notes/theology/meta-analysis-scholars]]","x":5680,"y":-1370,"width":330,"height":370,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"ecosystem-evangelical","type":"text","text":"## Evangelical Ecosystem\n\n**Organization:**\nETS (Evangelical Theological Society)\n\n**Requirement:**\nAnnual affirmation of biblical inerrancy\n\n**Key Journal:**\nJETS · Themelios\n\n**Key Institutions:**\nTEDS · Dallas · Westminster\nGordon-Conwell · Asbury · Wheaton\n\n**Key Publishers:**\nBaker Academic · Zondervan\nIVP Academic · B&H Academic\n\n**Strategy:** Publish in JBL/CBQ/VT\non technical topics (text crit, linguistics)\nAND in JETS/BBR on theological topics\n\n**Pete Enns Case (2008):**\nFault line WITHIN evangelicalism —\nhow far can critical engagement go?\n\n[[notes/theology/meta-analysis-scholars]]","x":4080,"y":-30,"width":330,"height":380,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"lemche","type":"text","text":"# Niels Peter Lemche\nCopenhagen (Emeritus)\n\n**Minimalist**\n\nDavid and Solomon are\nliterary figures\n\n*The Israelites in History\nand Tradition* (1998)\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":3945,"y":-627,"width":300,"height":355,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"hess","type":"text","text":"# Richard S. Hess\nDenver Seminary\n\n**Evangelical**\n\n5-point critique of Smith's\n*Early History of God* (Themelios 1992):\n\n- Smith assumes late monotheism\n- El ≠ always a personal name\n- Imagery sharing ≠ worship\n- No parallel for pantheon reduction\n- Asherah refs may be cult objects\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":5710,"y":1920,"width":300,"height":270,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"walton","type":"text","text":"# John H. Walton\nWheaton College\n\n**Evangelical**\n\n*Ancient Near Eastern Thought\nand the Old Testament* (2006)\n\nIsraelites shared ANE cognitive\nenvironment but had radically\ndifferent theology\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":3280,"y":3760,"width":300,"height":410,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"kitchen","type":"text","text":"# Kenneth A. Kitchen\n1932–2024 · Liverpool\n\n**Evangelical**\n\n*On the Reliability of the\nOld Testament* (2003)\n\nMassive defense of biblical\nhistoricity from Egyptian\nand ANE evidence\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":2980,"y":2800,"width":300,"height":375,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"longman","type":"text","text":"# Tremper Longman III\nWestmont College\n\n**Evangelical**\n\nCo-author: *A Biblical History\nof Israel* (2003)\n\nMethodological skepticism about\nminimalist and evolutionary approaches\n\nThreshold figure — bridges\nboth evangelical and critical worlds\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":-260,"y":2320,"width":300,"height":250,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"block","type":"text","text":"# Daniel I. Block\nWheaton College\n\n**Evangelical**\n\n*The Gods of the Nations* (1988/2000)\n\nIsrael's transcendent territorial\nclaim is genuinely distinctive\nin the ANE\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":1890,"y":1840,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pete-enns","type":"text","text":"## Pete Enns Case (2008)\n\n**Fault line within evangelicalism**\n\n*Inspiration and Incarnation* (2005):\nEvangelicals MUST accept the human,\nculturally-conditioned nature of Scripture\n\n**What happened:**\nSuspended, then departed from\nWestminster Theological Seminary\n\n**Why it matters:**\n\nIllustrates the DEEPEST divide —\nnot between evangelical and critical\nscholarship, but WITHIN evangelicalism\n\nBetween those who believe critical\nmethods are compatible with orthodoxy\nand those who don't\n\nParallel ecosystems don't just separate\nevangelicals from critical scholars —\nthey police boundaries INSIDE\nevangelicalism\n\n**Since:** Senior Fellow at BioLogos;\nwrites for popular audience about\nfaith-scholarship integration\n\n[[notes/theology/meta-analysis-scholars]]","x":1780,"y":805,"width":330,"height":390,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"heiser","type":"text","text":"# Michael S. Heiser\n1963–2023 · Faithlife Corp.\n\n**Divine Council framework**\n\n*The Unseen Realm* (2015)\n\n*Elohim* = place-of-residence term\nOther gods = created divine beings\nNOT co-eternal rival deities\n\nAgrees Deut 32:8 originally\n\"sons of God\" — interprets differently\n\nPhD UW-Madison (legit secular)\nbut outside citation network\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]\n[[notes/theology/meta-analysis-scholars]]","x":4880,"y":-2030,"width":300,"height":330,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"kaufmann","type":"text","text":"# Yehezkel Kaufmann\n1889–1963 · Hebrew Univ.\n\n**The Early Monotheism Pioneer**\n\n*Toledot ha-emunah ha-yisreelit*\n(8 vols, 1937–1956)\n\nMonotheism = REVOLUTION, not evolution\nMosaic, original, sui generis break\n\nP earliest (reverses Documentary Hyp.)\nTorah = pre-prophetic, pre-exilic\n\nMOST CITED + MOST CONTRADICTED\nin the entire debate\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":655,"y":-4760,"width":300,"height":330,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"kaufmann-paradox","type":"text","text":"## Kaufmann Paradox\n\n**Most cited + most contradicted**\n\n**The paradox:**\n\nKaufmann's work is impossible to ignore —\nevery major scholar engages him —\nbut almost nobody agrees with him\n\n**Evidence edges (green):**\n- Israel's Bible misrepresents paganism\n  as fetishism — genuine insight\n- Jeremiah-Deuteronomy literary\n  dependence (200+ citations)\n- Prophets don't accuse Israel of\n  pagan THEOLOGY\n\n**Conclusion edges (red):**\n- Circular definition of \"genuine polytheism\"\n- Treats theological consistency as\n  historical evidence\n- P-as-earliest contradicted by linguistics\n- Never explains WHERE Mosaic\n  monotheism came from\n- Kuntillet Ajrud (posthumous)\n\n**37+ contradict edges in graph**\n**0 support edges from other scholars**\n\n[[notes/theology/meta-analysis-scholars]]","x":2000,"y":-5520,"width":330,"height":440,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"zevit","type":"text","text":"# Ziony Zevit\nb. 1942 · Amer. Jewish Univ.\n\n**Parallactic synthesis**\n\n*The Religions of Ancient Israel* (2001)\n\nEvidence is messier than\nEITHER camp acknowledges\n\nMore cautious about grand\nnarratives than Smith\n\nKuntillet Ajrud: \"his asherah\"\nmay be cult object, not goddess\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":1480,"y":-4425,"width":300,"height":270,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"sommer","type":"text","text":"# Benjamin D. Sommer\nJewish Theological Seminary\n\n**Third way: Divine Fluidity**\n\n*The Bodies of God* (2009, Cambridge UP)\n\nGod has \"fluid self\" — multiple\nsimultaneous bodies while\nremaining one deity\n\nNOT polytheism — different ontology\n\nBetween Kaufmann and Smith\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":3140,"y":-4000,"width":300,"height":280,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"kugel","type":"text","text":"# James L. Kugel\nHarvard / Bar-Ilan (Emeritus)\n\n**Phenomenological critique**\n\n*The God of Old* (2003)\n*The Great Shift* (2017)\n\nConsensus model is reductive —\nfocuses on \"how many gods\"\nmisses HOW ancients experienced\nthe divine qualitatively\n\n\"Lost world\" of immediate\ndivine encounter\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":4440,"y":-3080,"width":300,"height":260,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"tigay","type":"text","text":"# Jeffrey H. Tigay\nUniv. of Pennsylvania\n\n**Strongest empirical challenge**\n\n*You Shall Have No Other Gods* (1986)\n\nOnomastics: 90%+ YHWH names\nin Hebrew inscriptions (8th–6th c.)\n\nSamaria: 100% · Lachish: 100%\nArad: 100% · Seals: 94%+\n\nWidespread monolatry centuries\nBEFORE exile — contradicts timeline\n\n[[notes/theology/scholarly-directory-yahweh-origins]]","x":4000,"y":-5445,"width":300,"height":290,"color":"6"}
	],
